From: Akisaira <akisaira@outlook.com>
Subject: [PATCH] usb: xhci: don't fail system suspend on a dead host

Nothing suspends the root hubs of a host that died: usb_hc_died() marks
them NOTATTACHED and usb_suspend_both() skips those, so hcd->state never
gets to HC_STATE_SUSPENDED. xhci_suspend() then returns -EINVAL, and
every system suspend aborts until the next reboot. A USB controller that
is of no use anyway shouldn't keep the whole machine awake.

Return 0 for a host in XHCI_STATE_DYING, after stopping the root hub
timers because the parent turns the clocks off next. Leave xhci_resume()
out for it as well: nothing was saved, and its reset path would clear
XHCI_STATE_DYING through xhci_start() and run the controller under an
hcd that stays dead, as HCD_FLAG_DEAD is never cleared.

Signed-off-by: Akisaira <akisaira@outlook.com>
Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
Origin: local
Upstream-Status: Pending
---
 drivers/usb/host/xhci.c | 21 +++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 21 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/usb/host/xhci.c b/drivers/usb/host/xhci.c
index 5c759ad28..92b50d01c 100644
--- a/drivers/usb/host/xhci.c
+++ b/drivers/usb/host/xhci.c
@@ -959,6 +959,20 @@ int xhci_suspend(struct xhci_hcd *xhci, bool do_wakeup)
 	if (!hcd->state)
 		return 0;
 
+	/*
+	 * Nothing suspends the root hubs of a dead host, so hcd->state never
+	 * gets to HC_STATE_SUSPENDED, and failing here would abort every system
+	 * suspend until the next reboot. xhci_hc_died() callers left it halted
+	 * or gone, so there is nothing to save. Only make sure no root hub
+	 * timer reads the ports once the parent has turned the clocks off.
+	 */
+	if (xhci->xhc_state & XHCI_STATE_DYING) {
+		timer_delete_sync(&hcd->rh_timer);
+		if (xhci->shared_hcd)
+			timer_delete_sync(&xhci->shared_hcd->rh_timer);
+		return 0;
+	}
+
 	if (hcd->state != HC_STATE_SUSPENDED ||
 	    (xhci->shared_hcd && xhci->shared_hcd->state != HC_STATE_SUSPENDED))
 		return -EINVAL;
@@ -1088,6 +1102,13 @@ int xhci_resume(struct xhci_hcd *xhci, bool power_lost, bool is_auto_resume)
 	if (!hcd->state)
 		return 0;
 
+	/*
+	 * xhci_suspend() saved nothing for a dead host, and the reset path below
+	 * would clear XHCI_STATE_DYING and start it again under a dead hcd.
+	 */
+	if (xhci->xhc_state & XHCI_STATE_DYING)
+		return 0;
+
 	/* Wait a bit if either of the roothubs need to settle from the
 	 * transition into bus suspend.
 	 */
